# Detached signatures cover the exact bytes of the file they sign, so these
# paths must never be end-of-line normalized. Git checks LF-stored text out as
# CRLF on Windows by default; that rewrite changes the signed bytes and the
# catalog stops verifying. It presents as CatalogTrustResult.BadSignature on
# Windows only, while Linux and macOS verify the same commit fine.
examples/catalog.json      -text
examples/catalog.json.sig  -text

# Signature and key material generally: bytes, not text.
*.sig   binary
*.priv  binary
*.pub   binary

# Firmware images are compared byte-for-byte against a catalog SHA-256.
*.elf   binary
*.hex   binary
